title: Genesis 9 – Blessings, Commandments and Promises
description: A study in Genesis 9: God blesses Noah and his sons, gives meat and the death penalty, sets the bow in the cloud, and Noah curses Canaan.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-9-blessings-and-covenant.html

=== Introduction
--- Blessings, Commandments and Promises [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 9
sub: God’s covenant with Noah and every living thing, and the curse of Canaan.
refs: Genesis 9:1-17
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

--- The pattern of God
lead: God blesses Noah and his sons, gives commandments, and makes a covenant with all living things in the earth.
panel: Blessings | Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth. [[Genesis 9:1]]
panel: Commandments | Eat not the blood; whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed. [[Genesis 9:4-6]]
panel: Promises | The waters shall no more become a flood to destroy all flesh. [[Genesis 9:15]]
center: This is the pattern of things with God when those who are faithful and saved by His grace walk with God.

=== Commandments
--- Every moving thing shall be meat
scripture: Genesis 9:1-4 | mark: Every moving thing that liveth shall be meat for you; even as the green herb; flesh with the life thereof, which is the blood thereof, shall ye not eat
- God tells Noah and his sons to be fruitful and multiply, birthing all nations of man. To that end, He reminds them that all animals are meat to eat, with no restrictions.
- Of the clean and unclean animals they may eat, but only the clean for sacrifice to God, being they represent Christ Jesus. [[Genesis 7:2]] [[Genesis 8:20]]
- But they must drain the blood, the life thereof. Of that they should not eat.

--- Done away in Christ
lead: The freedom given to Noah was replaced for a time for Israel with strict dietary laws against eating unclean beasts under Mosaic law, which, along with the priestly and carnal ordinances, were done away with in Christ.
scripture: Hebrews 9:10 | mark: carnal ordinances, imposed on them until the time of reformation
refs: Leviticus 11:1-8; Colossians 2:16-17; 1 Timothy 4:3-5

--- Blood for blood
big: Genesis 9:5-6 | mark: Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed; for in the image of God made he man
p: God institutes the death penalty, capital punishment for the shedding of blood. Before the flood, from Cain on, the requirement for blood didn’t exist, and evil propagated. Here God established a new understanding for man: that we were to enforce His law, blood for blood, *for in the image of God made he man*. [[Genesis 4:15]] [[Genesis 6:11]]

--- Bring forth abundantly
big: Genesis 9:7
center: God commands again that man be fruitful and multiply. Replenish the earth, bringing forth life abundantly.

=== The bow in the cloud
--- My covenant with you
scripture: Genesis 9:8-11 | mark: neither shall there any more be a flood to destroy the earth
p: God promises all life that He would never destroy the earth and all living things again by flood.

--- The token of the covenant
scripture: Genesis 9:12-17 | mark: I do set my bow in the cloud; that I may remember the everlasting covenant
center: He gives the rainbow as His reminder, a token of the covenant between Him and the earth.

=== The sons of Noah
--- Of them was the whole earth overspread
scripture: Genesis 9:18-19 | mark: Ham is the father of Canaan; of them was the whole earth overspread
p: The Bible tells us of Shem, and Ham, and Japheth, and that Ham is the father of Canaan. Of these three was the whole earth overspread. The next chapter of Genesis goes into detail of the generations and nations of them, but for the rest of chapter 9 we need to know Ham’s son Canaan. [[lesson:genesis-10-table-of-nations|Genesis 10]]

--- Noah’s wine
scripture: Genesis 9:20-23
p: Noah, retired from ark building, becomes a husbandman, a grower of grapes. The Bible says he drank his own wine and became drunk, that Ham saw his nakedness as he was passed out in his tent, and that he told his brothers.
note: Wine is a mocker. [[Proverbs 20:1]] [[lesson:topic-walk-wine|Wine and strong drink]]

--- What his younger son had done
big: Genesis 9:24-25
p: There is a lot of speculation as to what this means. Most agree that Ham did something unspeakable to Noah in his condition. The Bible doesn’t say that, and generally God’s word isn’t shy about naming the acts done by the wicked. The implication comes from Noah’s reaction and punishment, which is severe.

--- Blessed and cursed
scripture: Genesis 9:26-27
panel: Shem | Blessed with the blessing of the {Lord} God, as the oldest. This is the blessing of Christ through his seed. [[Luke 3:36]]
panel: Japheth | Blessed with abundance, to be enlarged greatly.
panel-warn: Canaan | Ham’s son Canaan cursed to be a servant of servants unto his brethren, Shem and Japheth: the nations that spring from each son.
note: There is a lot of speculative theology based off this curse, and some of the conclusions drawn aren’t supported in scripture. Take secular takes on a spiritual matter with the appropriate grains of salt.

--- The last of the long-lived men
scripture: Genesis 9:28-29
stat: 350 | years Noah lived after the flood
stat: 950 | years in all
center: He is the last of the antediluvian long-lived men.

=== The spiritual application
--- What’s important
lead: There are deeper things of God here: His promises and blessings, the salvation of Christ mirroring the salvation of the ark.
panel-warn: Flooded out | The predominantly secular focus on hidden meaning, esoteric knowledge, the hyperfocus on race and genealogies of man, conspiracies and Jewish fables have all but flooded out those truths in the minds of man. Even saved Christians get sucked in to endless strivings about the meaning of some of what’s revealed to us. [[Titus 1:14]] [[1 Timothy 1:4]]
panel: Draw spiritual application | Understand the things of God which He revealed to us from the beginning. Mercy, judgment, grace and salvation. The fallen nature of man and the prevalence of sin while we are in the flesh. The righteousness of the living God.

--- Give thanks [title]
overline: Genesis 9
heading: Give thanks
p: As we give thanks to God for our salvation and the blessings He bestows, the same way Noah gave thanks after leaving the ark, we should keep in mind the spiritual, looking forward to that better country and the feast of Christ Jesus, knowing that man’s relationship with God has always been, from the beginning. Amen. [[Hebrews 11:16]] [[Revelation 19:9]]

=== Close
--- Blessings, commandments and promises [title]
overline: Genesis 9
point: Meat, but not the blood | Every moving thing is meat. The dietary law came later for Israel and was done away in Christ.
point: Blood for blood | God gave man the sword to enforce His law, for in the image of God made He man.

--- Blessings, commandments and promises, continued
point: The bow in the cloud | God remembers His covenant, and the waters shall no more become a flood.
point: Draw spiritual application | Not endless strivings, but mercy, judgment, grace and salvation.

